# Model routing and scope gates

## Goal

Keep model choice aligned with task type, and pause to confirm model switches when scope grows.

## Recommended routing

- `cad-architecture-doc-review` → Gemini 3.1 Pro
- `cad-architecture-solid-dry`:
  - review/design tradeoffs → Gemini 3.1 Pro
  - implementation/refactor/code edits → GPT 5.3 Codex
- `cad-cpp-performance-opengl` → GPT 5.3 Codex
- `cad-cross-platform-cmake` → GPT 5.3 Codex
- `cad-feature-workflow`:
  - main implementation flow → GPT 5.3 Codex
  - small follow-up edits/log touch-ups → GPT 5.4 Mini
- `cad-naming-style` → GPT 5.4 Mini

## Sub-agents (Task tool)

When spawning a sub-agent for work that matches a skill above, **prefer the same model routing** as for the parent (implementation → GPT 5.3 Codex, architecture/review → Gemini 3.1 Pro, small edits → GPT 5.4 Mini). If the user does not specify a model on the sub-agent, pick the route that matches the sub-task type.

## Credit / budget constraints

Ideal routing is **not** mandatory when credits are tight. If the user says they are **low on credits**, **out of credits**, or to use **Auto** (or they have already chosen Auto for the session), **do not nag** to switch models — proceed with the current or Auto-selected model. Only suggest an upgrade when it would clearly reduce rework (e.g. large refactor) and a single short nudge is enough.

## Before execution

- If current model does not match recommended routing **and** the user has not indicated credit/budget constraints or Auto, ask: `Current model is <X>; recommended is <Y> for this task. Switch now?`
- If task scope is unclear, do a quick discovery pass first (inspect likely impacted files/modules), then confirm model choice.

## Small vs big edits (scope gate)

- Treat as **small** only if isolated and reversible, usually in 1-2 files.
- Escalate to **big** when any trigger appears:
  - touches 3+ files or crosses module boundaries
  - changes interfaces/contracts or public behavior
  - needs broad test updates or non-trivial validation
  - affects CMake/build/resources/shaders/platform concerns
  - touches render/update hot paths or performance-sensitive code
  - reveals significant ambiguity or multiple architectural options

## Mandatory pause-and-ask

- If a task starts small but hits any escalation trigger, stop before major edits and ask to switch to the recommended stronger model **unless** the user is credit-limited or on Auto (then continue with the current model and flag risk briefly).
- If the recommended model is **unavailable** (not in the picker, policy block, etc.) and the user has **not** said to use Auto or accept budget limits, ask how to proceed.
- If the user prefers **Auto** or is **credit-limited**, treat Auto or the current model as acceptable and continue without blocking on the ideal map.
